Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-10-2000||09:35 PM||||  Hey y'all, I was wondering if there is a fix for sluggish windows and door locks? My windows go up and down ok, but man are they slow <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> Same with the door locks. It takes four or five attempts to finaly get them locked or unlocked using the power lock system <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> These things are by no means an emergency, but it would be cool <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"> to get them fixed at this stage of my project. <P>  Thanx To All <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>  BAM-BAM||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ed||03-10-2000||11:23 PM||||I fixed my power door locks about a month ago. Take off the door panels and lubricate all the moving parts in the lock linkage. <P>One "trick", though. When you remove the panels using a flat blade screwdriver or the special panel removing tool available at parts houses, note that probably one of the plastic panel fasteners will be shorter than the others to allow the window to pass. Other broken fasteners can be replaced with readily available general fasteners.<P>I haven't tried lubricating my power windows because a lot of the mechanism is behind a metal panel that is held on with rivets you have to drill out. A little part of the mechanism is available at the rear of the door, however, and can be easily lubricated. ||||reg||1
